  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.\r\rReason: This is required by Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).",
    "The facing materials used in the development to which this permission relates shall match those of the existing building(s) unless otherwise agreed in writing by the local planning authority.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance on completion of the development, in accordance with policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policies CS8 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The use to which this permission relates shall not open outside of the following hours:\r\r7am to 11pm Monday to Sunday including Bank Holidays\r\rReason: To ensure satisfactory living conditions for neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012",
    "The works shall be carried out and maintained in accordance with the deposited Reasonable Exception Statement compliant with Policy D12(A).\r\rReason: In the interests of fire safety and to ensure the safety of all building users in accordance with Policy D12 (Fire Safety) of the London Plan 2021.",
    "If, during the implementation of the development hereby approved (including demolition, structural clearance, or roof dismantling works), any unexpected protected species or distinct ecological assets are discovered on-site, all building works must cease immediately. A professional survey conducted by a suitably qualified ecologist, alongside a comprehensive mitigation strategy, must be submitted to the Local Planning Authority for written endorsement. No further construction footprints or alterations shall be advanced until the approved mitigation measures have been fully implemented.\r\rReason: To ensure the continuous protection of localised biodiversity assets and wild habitats during construction phases, in accordance with the National Planning Policy Framework and Core Strategy requirements."
  ],
